# PVC Design Rules (English Canonical)

> Korean siblings: `design/design-system.mdc`, `typography-korean.mdc`, `accessibility.mdc`.

## 1. Design System First

- Build UI from shared tokens/components, not one-off page styles.
- Tokenize color, type, space, radius, elevation, motion, state.
- Reuse buttons/inputs/modals/tables/alerts; minimize inline/arbitrary colors and meaningless class names.
- Same semantics → same component/language/color meaning across screens.
- Keep `docs/design/` (or equivalent) current; update CODEMAP when the system changes.

## 2. Typography (incl. Korean)

- Single source: `TYPEGUIDE.md` / design docs; sizes/line-height/weight via tokens.
- Keep KR+EN mixed layouts readable; consistent role scale (title/body/caption/label).
- Don’t break layout on wrapping/ellipsis/long Korean strings; preserve readability on small screens.
- Changing type tokens requires checking key screens + docs.

## 3. Accessibility

- Semantic HTML, keyboard use, visible focus, contrast, alt text, clear errors by default.
- Reference **WCAG 2.2**; adapt only when real user/device constraints require it.
- Clickable ⇒ keyboard operable; manage focus in dialogs/menus.
- Don’t convey state by color alone; keep responsive operability; verify a11y in done checklist.
